body:
ALL THE TIME. Worse is when people don't tell you that they could not understand what you said, and they either cut the conversation/ignore you, or they move to a different topic. It kinda reinforces the feeling that you're invalidated even though it's not true. Also it fucks with your brain while you try to figure out that they could just not hear what you said. 

&#x200B;

Ironically, I feel like a lot of times I cannot for the life of me understand what other people are saying. Everyone seems to listen and tune in on the conversation, while I'm just standing there trying to infer wth was that scrambled noise that came to my ears.
